
    Approximation of π by Monte Carlo method

    Analysis:
        A circle with radius r is inscribed within a
        square with edges of length 2.  The area of the
        square is thus 4, while the area of the circle
        is a=πr².  The probability a random point will
        fall within the circle is thus:
                p = a/4 = πr²/4
        Given an empirical measure of the probability,
        we can compute an estimate of π as:
                π ≅ 4p / r²

